course: dictionary
lesson: 4861
title: The word ending -ic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ic is not a word you can use on its own. It is a word ending, called a suffix. Add it to the end of a word and it makes a describing word: hero becomes heroic, and atom becomes atomic. The ending -ic means of or like.
explain: Words ending in -ic often change again when they become adverbs, the words that tell you how something is done. «Words ending in -ic add -ally: basic, basically; dramatic, dramatically» shows the pattern. Basic becomes basically, and dramatic becomes dramatically.
explain: Be careful: «publicly» is the exception. It takes -ly, not -ally. When you meet an -ic word, check the sentence and ask whether your new word fits.
fact: -ic is a suffix, a word ending that makes describing words such as magic, heroic, metallic and athletic.
fact: -ic means of or like, so heroic means like a hero.
fact: IC stands for integrated circuit, a tiny electronic chip found in many computers and phones.
fact: In some places, I/C means in charge.
fact: On its own, ic is not an English word, so you will not find it in a sentence by itself.
exercise: «Words ending in -ic add -ally: basic, basically.» What do you add to basic to make basically? | -ness | -ful | -ic | *-ally
exercise: What does the suffix -ic mean? | *of or like | a tiny chip | a full stop | in charge
exercise: Which spelling is the exception to the -ally rule? | *publicly | basically | heroically | dramatically
test: What does IC stand for in computing? | in charge of a class | *integrated circuit | ice cream | internal code
test: Which word is an adjective made with the suffix -ic? | *metallic | icing | ticket | metal
exam: What is the adverb of heroic? | heroicly | heroicing | heroics | *heroically
